   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## H3 Perfect Loop - Bridge route\n\nOne queue press renders the whole loop:\n\n1. **Clip A** is a normal FL2VA generation from your start image (unwire `first_frame` for pure t2va).\n2. **H3 Loop Bridge** pins a second generation's head to A's last frames and its tail to A's FIRST frames - sliced straight out of A's sampler latent, no decode/re-encode, sound included. The bridge's middle is free generation that leaves A the way it ends and arrives at A's opening the way it begins: the wrap itself, generated.\n3. **H3 Loop Splice** cuts the pinned spans and joins A + middle. The result loops back to A's frame 0 seamlessly.\n\n**Prompts:** clip A's prompt is your shot; the bridge prompt should describe the same scene with motion that can return home (\"...the motion settles back to where it began\"). Keep CFG 1 / BasicGuider (community-standard for H3; Turbo LoRAs assume it).\n\n**Knobs:** `head_frames`/`tail_frames` 22 is the chaining sweet spot. If a faint shimmer survives at either join, set `video_blend_frames` 3-6 on the splice. `pin_mode` `conditioning_rows` is the field-proven mechanism; `latent_mask` is leaner and makes the cuts bit-exact - try both.\n\n**Check the seam** with the second Save: it plays the loop rolled by half, so the wrap sits mid-clip where a normal player can show it.\n\nModels: Comfy-Org H3 packaging (fl2va UNet, minimax CLIP, video + audio VAE) in their usual folders."
   ],
   "title": "README"
  },
